  "item": "impl[Memory/Graph]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This validation fixture stores records directly by opaque u8 node ID.\n Its in-memory EvidenceStorage does not translate IDs into filesystem\n paths; Graph still requires the addressing callback. Filesystem storage\n and its consumer delegation tests exercise path-based storage separately."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#impl[Memory/Graph]/fn[node_path]` is a fenced commentary citation on an explicit function, which is a permitted form. The commentary gives a substantive reason why zero execution is acceptable, and it agrees with the current source:\n\n- **Fixture storage:** `Memory` keeps records by opaque `u8` ID, and its `EvidenceStorage` impl (`load_evidence` and related methods) looks records up by node. It does not translate IDs into paths.\n- **Why the callback exists:** `Graph::node_path` is a required trait method, so the fixture has to implement it.\n- **Only the agent tool code calls it:** in the sources I searched, the only non-test callers of `node_path` are in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs`. The `MockAgent` in `validation.rs` does not call it, so this fixture never needs the callback.\n- **Path-based behavior is tested elsewhere:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs` has a consumer fixture whose `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` delegate through `node_path`. Its test `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` exercises that. `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs` has a test that asserts `node_path` behavior.\n\nThe explanation is prose, not difficulty alone. It is not redundant with any other role citation.",
